docs/backlog-archive.md:138:| 2026-08-08 | **Task 717 (Sprint 52.2) — ✅ `APPROVED` (orchestrator review 2026-08-08). Sprint 52 advances to 52.3.** The bare-directory `src/design-system/mantine` token exemption is gone, replaced by **11 exact-file keys** (zero directories) plus per-line `design-tokens-allow` markers. The 206/15 baseline was re-derived with the detector's own exports and matched the kickoff exactly; all 206 literals were classified **141 `createTheme()` input / 40 non-tokenized affordance / 25 genuine N1**, and the 25 were **reserved under 734, not remediated** — the split the kickoff's R8 required. The deferral is disclosed at every site rather than papered over: two allowlist keys open with `RESERVED for Task 734 (genuine N1 violation, not remediated here)` and 18 markers say `genuine N1, reserved Task 734` in their own reason text. `isAllowlisted`'s unbounded third arm (`relPath.startsWith(key)`) was removed after re-measuring 0 dependents, so the new exact-file keys finally have a boundary. Plant proven on `slider-chrome.css` — deliberately a file with **zero** pre-existing literals, so the planted violation is unambiguous: the gate reported `Total: 1 raw style-value violation(s)` naming the file, then returned to 0 with `git hash-object` back at `42adc4198…` and an empty porcelain. **Reviewer re-verified R7 independently rather than accepting the executor's filtered diff:** all 34 changed line pairs are code-identical with only an appended marker comment, so "zero rendered value change" is structurally true and the `Q1` profile is correctly chosen. `check:design-tokens:strict` 0 violations / 0 stale-marker / 0 missing-reason; `tsc`, `build`, `check:i18n`, both integrity passes exit 0. **Review finding F1 — the contested classification is right, and understated.** `MantineResponsiveActionFooter.tsx:41` puts `zIndex: 100` on a `position:sticky` element: that is `--z-toast`, 70 above the semantically-matching `--z-sticky: 30`, and above `--z-overlay: 40`, `--z-modal: 50` and `--z-popover: 50`. The repo's own sticky convention corroborates it — `AdminMobileHeader.tsx:41` and `AdminPageShell.tsx:30` both use `z-30`. It is **latent, not live**: no production consumer passes `sticky`, only the Storybook story renders it. Consequence carried into 734: correcting it moves the footer below overlay/modal/popover, so it is a **behavioural** change needing a rendered witness, not a mechanical token swap. **F2 (P3):** the report says 44 markers; 43 marker occurrences exist across 34 lines — immaterial, since one marker value legitimately suppresses several detections on a shorthand line, and the gate's 0 stale-marker / 0 missing-reason is the real completeness proof. **F3:** the OQ1 call (23 per-line markers in `input-chrome.css` rather than a file-level reserved key) is accepted — a file-level key would have re-exempted the ~70% that are legitimately justified, which is the blanket shape this task exists to remove. | 717 | `docs/sessions/2026-08-08-task717-design-tokens-allowlist-narrowing.md` |
docs/backlog-reserved.md:28:| 734 | reserved — filed by 717 | **25 genuine N1 violations inside `src/design-system/mantine`, reserved not remediated (R7).** `typography.ts` (3, `SECTION_HEADING_FZ`) · `input-chrome.css` (7, padding matching `--space-2-5`/`--space-4` exactly) · `MantineListingCardPattern.module.css` (12: 4× `transition` matching `--duration-slow` exactly, 8× `.card:hover` box-shadow duplicating the Mantine-generated `--mantine-shadow-lg` var the sibling `.premium:hover` rule already references) · `MantineDialogDrawerPattern.tsx` + `responsiveBottomSheet.tsx` (1 each, `paddingBottom` matching `--space-2`) · `MantineResponsiveActionFooter.tsx` (1, `zIndex: 100` bypassing the semantically-named `--z-sticky`). Per-file counts above are the durable record; the per-line table is **local-only** (`.screenshots/task717-evidence/I3-classification.md`, D6) so **734 re-derives the census rather than depending on it** — the 711/728 lesson. **Review escalation (2026-08-08):** `MantineResponsiveActionFooter`'s `zIndex: 100` is not a plain tokenization item — it is `--z-toast` on a `position:sticky` element, above `--z-overlay`/`--z-modal`/`--z-popover`, while the repo's own sticky convention is `z-30` (`AdminMobileHeader.tsx:41`, `AdminPageShell.tsx:30`). Latent only because no production consumer passes `sticky`. Correcting it **moves the element down 70 layers**, so that item alone needs a rendered witness and a Q2/Q3 arm, and 734 must state whether the answer is `--z-sticky` or a new token. |
